Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-08-2001||03:38 PM||||Having some problems with this. At the end it says "Either your not connected to the internet (I nkow I am, I'm using cable) or you are having a proxy problem". Does @home use a proxy, and if so, where would I find the address that I have to type in?||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||03-08-2001||04:10 PM||||Check your browser setup (under tools -&gt; internet options -&gt; connections under IE 5.0) and look for any reference to proxy servers and/or automatic proxy server detection, if either are set turn them off and see what happens. <P>If you go to your @home home page or try <A HREF="http://www.rr.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rr.com</A>  and poke around you may find what they want your default proxy server settings to be. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrRodey||03-08-2001||09:52 PM||||You'd be a lot better off using Lime Wire.  It has just as many if not more options then i-mesh, And it doesn't run off of a central server like both Napster and I-mesh do.  Thusly you can't get kicked off, and they aren't involved in the copyright cases like Napster.  ||||reg||1
