Z||000006||btoth||03-09-2001||10:43 AM||||imesh is screwy sometimes.  if you have problems connecting, or get disconnected frequently, or just can't get the darned thing to run on your computer... try turning off hardware acceleration in your display settings under "trouble shooting".  i've had to do this the fist time i would run imesh after installing and then if i turn hardware accel. back on it seems to work fine.  (i don't know why this would change anything though.)<P><BR>to get music though, you can't beat napster.<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000007||Shaft||03-09-2001||05:51 PM||||If you're on a netwrok with a firewall like I am then you'll need to use a program called socks5. Then when typing in your server type socks5.servername...||||reg||1
